        "description": "Explanation calculation climate risk score: Original data about implementation of adaptation measure are from Zhao et al.1 and for climate risks from Trnka et al.2and are given per climate zone. These were aggregated to country scale using the area share of the climate zones.\n\nZhao et al.1 reported the results of a survey among farmers into (i) the extent to which they have already taken measures (because of evident effects of climate change) and (ii) the extent to which they plan to take additional measures. Both i and ii can be seen as indicators of the risk “perception” of the farming community. For this we used a variant with all measures accounted for and one with a selection.\n\nFrom Trnka et al.2 we took modeled climate changes for the year 2030 and a translation thereof into changes in (i) the length of the growing season and (ii) the number of (too) dry days. We also calculated sensitivities using the changes in agro-climatic indicators change in length of the growing season and of number of dry days). Here the score runs from positive (climate benefits) to negative (climate costs)\n\nWe found a good correlation (r2=0.77 between climate risk indices derived from Zhao et al. (2022), using the selection of taken measures, and derived from Trnka et al. (2011). The selection of measures focuses on choice of cultivar and hydrologic measures.",
